    <div class="w-layout-grid grid">
      <div id="w-node-_1c423e5f-43ae-ca26-9b28-dbb78dcfcdd9-f89852d3" class="about what-we-do"></div>
      <div id="w-node-fffcdbaa-d7a7-3f60-bb70-88c1a94e1b9a-f89852d3">
        <h1 class="h2"><strong class="bold-text-2">Who</strong> we Are</h1>
        <div>The Nigeria Seeds Information management system NIGSIMS, is  a technology enabled service for the liberalization of the seed marketplace in Nigeria.This is a  Feed the Future RRA Activity  funded by USAID, implemented by Mercy Corps in partnership with Save the Children International and International Fertilizer Development Center (IFDC) is to facilitate and protect economic recovery and growth in vulnerable conflict-affected areas and increase incomes, improve livelihood and resilience of households 
The system has a synergy across different players such as  Farmers, Seed traders, Seed companies and National Agricultural Seed Council regulations.(NASC) traders with an overall goal of ensuring the distribution of quality seeds to farmers. 
<br><br>NIGSIMS is committed to liberating and redefining the business processes in the agricultural ecosystem.<br></div>
      </div>
      <div id="w-node-_27884092-f777-2dab-20b2-0315bcf50154-f89852d3" class="div-block-13">
        <h1 class="h2"><strong class="bold-text-3">What</strong> We Do</h1>
        <div>NIGSIMS is committed to automating and facilitating an efficient distribution network of quality and certified seeds to farmers that ensures an agriculture-led growth in the economy of the country as well as a sustainable reduction in malnutrition and poverty in the initial target states of Adamawa, Borno, Gombe and Yobe States. .<br></div>
      </div>
      <div id="w-node-c271ba2b-e497-9efc-73ef-23000f57b89a-f89852d3" class="about what-we-do"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="div-block-12">
      <div>
        <h1 class="h2">Our <strong class="bold-text-4">Objectives</strong></h1>
      </div>
      <ul role="list" class="list">
        <li class="list-item">To assist the farmers by ensuring timely and adequate availability of certified/quality seeds of suitable varieties at reasonable prices.</li>
        <li class="list-item">To identify potential partners and innovative approaches that leverage the development of practical and market-driven solutions to implement innovative structures that target small-scale farmers, youth, women, and micro-enterprises.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Creation of a marketplace that will integrate 50 seed traders reaching over 5000 smallholder farmers through sales of 50mt seed and improved knowledge on seeds and good agronomic practices.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Liberalization of the seed ecosystem through automation of NASC certification process and development of business of at least 10 seed companies in the Northeast to enable more efficient seed distribution.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Increase access to seed and seed information to 5000 smallholder farmers through the set-up of seed support via call-center where farmers are able to enquire information about seed through different communication channels.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
